{
  "summary": "This study investigates breaking the capacity-reversibility trade-off in Li-O2 batteries using amorphous non-precious MnFeCoNiCu high-entropy alloy (A-HEA) catalysts. The researchers designed A-HEA via liquid-phase reduction to create a porous structure enhancing electrochemical surface area and promoting solution-mediated discharge pathways. The catalyst achieved 10.8 mAh cm-2 capacity with reduced overpotential (0.75 V) and extended cycle life 4-5 times versus crystalline analogs. The material demonstrated scalability and performance in pouch cells at high rates and low temperatures.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A-HEA catalyst achieved 10.8 mAh cm-2 discharge capacity",
    "Reduced overpotential to 0.75 V and 4-5x longer cycle life versus crystalline catalysts",
    "Scalable production and high-performance in pouch cells at 400 mA and -30°C"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a non-precious catalyst strategy to overcome the fundamental capacity-reversibility trade-off in Li-O2 batteries, enabling higher energy density and longer cycle life without compromising reversibility."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated NLGP's immunomodulatory effects in NSCLC by assessing its impact on Treg-mediated immunosuppression and TH1 polarization. Using PBMCs from NSCLC patients and healthy controls, NLGP treatment enhanced lymphocyte proliferation, cytotoxic T lymphocyte activity, nitric oxide release, and type 1 cytokine production while reducing TH2, TH17, and Treg-associated gene expression. The results indicate NLGP shifts adaptive immunity toward a tumoricidal TH1 profile by suppressing Treg function.",
  "key_findings": [
    "NLGP enhanced lymphocyte proliferation and cytotoxic T lymphocyte activity in NSCLC patient PBMCs",
    "NLGP increased nitric oxide release and type 1 cytokine production while reducing TH2 and TH17 responses",
    "NLGP suppressed Treg-associated genes (IL10 and FOXP3) indicating reduced regulatory T cell function"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "NLGP demonstrates a mechanism for enhancing antitumor immunity in NSCLC by modulating T cell differentiation toward a tumoricidal TH1 response while inhibiting immunosuppressive regulatory T cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether transient dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with acute type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a 4-day high-fat diet (HFD) exposure at disease onset exacerbates inflammation comparably to chronic obesity. The effect is confined to a specific 4-day window; HFD outside this window has no impact. Switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the same window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. Neutrophil depletion, Nlrp3 deficiency, or NLRP3 inhibition mitigates inflammation. Post-recovery, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent LFD. The findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory through neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β axis activation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure at disease onset exacerbates acute type 17 skin inflammation in lean mice",
    "The inflammatory effect is restricted to a 4-day peri-initiation window; HFD outside this window has no impact",
    "Neutrophil-mediated NLRP3-IL-1β axis drives pathogenic TH17 cell activation, with post-recovery tissue-resident memory T cells persisting"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that short-lived dietary states during acute inflammation can durably reprogram tissue immune memory via neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β signaling, revealing a critical temporal window for dietary interventions to influence inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates spin-selective hydrogen utilization in Ag-modified chiral Cu electrocatalysts for efficient CO2-to-CH4 conversion. The researchers leveraged structural chirality to induce chirality-induced spin selectivity, which suppresses spin-singlet H2 formation and mitigates the competing hydrogen evolution reaction. Ag modification enhanced *CO intermediate supply, enabling a 67.0% CH4 Farada. The catalyst achieved unassisted solar-driven CO2-to-CH4 conversion with 54.1% CH4 FE and 5.86% solar-to-fuel efficiency.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Chiral Cu frameworks with Ag modification suppress HER by favoring spin-selective hydrogen utilization",
    "The catalyst achieves 67.0% CH4 Faradaic efficiency at -0.7 V vs. RHE",
    "Unassisted solar-driven CO2-to-CH4 conversion yields 54.1% CH4 FE and 5.86% solar-to-fuel efficiency"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates spin-selective hydrogen utilization as a viable strategy for selective hydrocarbon synthesis and bias-free solar CO2-to-fuel conversion."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used bidirectional two-sample Mendelian randomization to investigate causal relationships between 731 immune cell traits and hip osteoarthritis (HOA) risk. Analysis identified 17 immune traits with statistically significant associations (FDR < 0.05) in the forward direction, including six CD33-expressing myeloid traits positively associated with HOA risk and eleven lymphoid/monocyte traits inversely associated. Reverse analysis showed no robust evidence for HOA causing immune changes. Findings suggest potential immune-mediated HOA mechanisms but require experimental validation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Six CD33-expressing myeloid cell traits showed positive associations with HOA risk (odds ratio 1.02, 95% CI 1.01-1.03)",
    "Eleven immune traits including T cells, B cells, NK cells, regulatory T cells, and dendritic cells showed inverse associations with HOA risk (odds ratio range 0.90-0.97)",
    "Reverse MR analysis found no robust evidence for causal effects of HOA on immune cell composition after FDR correction"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study provides genetic evidence for immune cell traits influencing hip osteoarthritis risk through Mendelian randomization, advancing understanding of potential immunological pathways in osteoarthritis pathophysiology."
}

{
  "summary": "This review investigates multi-principal element alloys (MPEAs) for solid-state hydrogen storage, addressing challenges like poor thermodynamics, slow kinetics, and degradation. It establishes a composition-process-structure-property framework integrating computational modeling, machine learning, and experimental techniques to understand atomic-scale degradation mechanisms such as hydrogen-induced amorphization and surface poisoning. The study identifies design principles for high-capacity, durable systems with fast kinetics and low cost, offering pathways for scalable hydrogen storage applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MPEAs overcome hydrogen storage bottleneuses through atomic-scale design and synergistic effects",
    "Advanced characterization reveals mechanisms of hydrogen-induced amorphization and surface poisoning",
    "A unified framework links electronic structure to heat/mass transport for system-level optimization"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a foundational framework for designing robust, high-capacity solid-state hydrogen storage systems by elucidating atomic-scale degradation mechanisms and enabling multi-scale optimization strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether oral Bacillus subtilis could mitigate house dust mite-induced atopic dermatitis in mice. Using a murine model, the researchers administered B. subtilis and observed significant reductions in clinical symptoms at weeks 3 and 7. The probiotic also decreased skin mast cell counts and increased serum IgA levels, though effects on epidermal thickness were transient. No significant changes in HDM-specific IgE or regulatory T cells in lymph nodes were noted, but intestinal Treg frequencies rose post-treatment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Oral B. subtilis reduced clinical symptoms of house dust mite-induced atopic dermatitis in mice by weeks 3 and 7",
    "B. subtilis decreased skin mast cell numbers and increased serum IgA levels",
    "Intestinal regulatory T cell frequencies increased one week after treatment, though skin-draining lymph node Tregs remained unchanged"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that oral probiotic administration can modulate mucosal immunity and reduce atopic dermatitis severity through mechanisms involving intestinal regulatory T cells and IgA elevation, offering insights into bacterial tolerance induction in allergic diseases."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing zinc-iodine battery performance by resolving polyiodide shuttling and interfacial mass-transport issues. Using molecular catalyst screening, iron(III) meso-tetrakis(4-carboxyphenyl) porphyrin (Fe-TCPP) was identified as an interfacial regulator that stabilizes iodide intermediates without passivating the interface and promotes zinc ion accessibility. The Fe-TCPP-regulated cathode achieves 178 mAh g-1 capacity and 50,000 cycles at 5 A g-1, demonstrating effective synchronization of electron transfer and ion redistribution for long-term stability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fe-TCPP stabilizes iodide intermediates without interfacial passivation",
    "Peripheral carboxyphenyl groups enhance zinc ion accessibility",
    "The cathode achieves 178 mAh g-1 capacity and 50,000 cycles at 5 A g-1"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a molecular-catalytic strategy for simultaneously regulating redox-intermediate conversion and ion transport in aqueous zinc-iodine batteries, addressing a critical bottleneck for practical implementation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the role of IGF2BP3 in pancreatic adenocarcinoma (PAAD) by integrating multi-omics and experimental approaches. It identified IGF2BP3 as significantly upregulated in PAAD with poor prognosis, linked to MMP1, MMP7, and ITGA2 in ECM remodeling. IGF2BP3 knockdown reduced cell proliferation, migration, and invasion while decreasing transcript stability. The IGF2BP3-MMP7 axis correlated with regulatory T-cell infiltration and immunosuppressive niches, suggesting a mechanism for tumor immune evasion. Trametinib was highlighted as a potential therapeutic candidate for high-risk PAAD.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IGF2BP3 is significantly upregulated in pancreatic adenocarcinoma and associated with poor prognosis",
    "IGF2BP3 knockdown reduces proliferation, migration, and invasion of pancreatic cancer cells and decreases stability of ECM-related transcripts",
    "The IGF2BP3-MMP7 axis correlates with regulatory T-cell infiltration and immunosuppressive microenvironments in PAAD"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a mechanistic link between IGF2BP3-driven ECM remodeling and Treg-mediated immunosuppression in pancreatic adenocarcinoma, providing a potential targetable pathway for immunotherapy."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines scalable manufacturing challenges in flexible electronics, focusing on maintaining high performance during scale-up. It analyzes the interplay between material design, processing techniques, morphology evolution, and device integration for both planar and fiber-type systems. The study highlights strategies that preserve functional reliability while enabling large-area reproducibility, high yield, and throughput in commercial applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Scalable fabrication strategies maintain device performance during manufacturing scale-up",
    "Material design and processing techniques must synergistically optimize morphology evolution",
    "Planar and fiber-type flexible electronics require tailored approaches to ensure high-reproducibility systems"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a systematic framework for understanding how material selection and processing parameters interact to sustain high-performance flexible electronics during industrial-scale production."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated thioredoxin-1 (Trx-1) in MPTP-induced Parkinson's disease mice, focusing on its role in microglial immune responses. Trx-1 overexpression reduced microglial activation, pro-inflammatory cytokines, α-synuclein accumulation, and MHC-II-mediated antigen presentation. It also reversed MPTP-induced Th17 differentiation, FOXP3 suppression, and FOXO1 nuclear exclusion in the substantia nigra. These effects suggest Trx-1 promotes regulatory T cell differentiation to induce immune tolerance against α-synuclein presented by MHC-II in microglia, offering a potential neuroprotective mechanism for Parkinson's disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Trx-1 overexpression suppressed MPTP-induced microglial activation and pro-inflammatory cytokine production",
    "Trx-1 reduced α-synuclein accumulation and MHC-II-mediated antigen presentation in microglia",
    "Trx-1 reversed MPTP-induced Th17 differentiation, FOXP3 suppression, and FOXO1 nuclear exclusion in the substantia nigra"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study identifies thioredoxin-1 as a key regulator of microglial autoimmune responses in Parkinson's disease, providing mechanistic insight into how redox signaling can modulate neuroinflammation and immune tolerance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates quantum effects in electro-optic materials at cryogenic temperatures. By combining thermodynamic analysis, phase-field simulations, experimental growth, and cryogenic optical measurements, researchers demonstrated that quantum fluctuations can stabilize a large electro-optic response (reff = 2850 pm/V) near 0 K. The approach tuned ferroelectric phase boundaries to achieve temperature independence below 25 K, outperforming room-temperature and cryogenic benchmarks by orders of magnitude.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Quantum fluctuations enable temperature-independent electro-optic response below 25 K",
    "BaTiO3 on GdScO3 achieves reff = 2850 pm/V at cryogenic temperatures",
    "Ba0.77Ca0.23TiO3 shows r51 = 1898 pm/V, surpassing BaTiO3-on-Si by over an order of magnitude"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a quantum design principle for cryogenic electro-optic materials, overcoming traditional temperature sensitivity limitations through engineered phase boundaries."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines multi-transgene-armed oncolytic viruses (OVs) for cancer immunotherapy. It addresses how co-expressing multiple immunomodulatory transgenes—such as cytokines, immune checkpoint inhibitors, and T-cell activators—overcomes limitations of single-transgene OVs by enhancing dendritic cell maturation, CD8+ T cell infiltration, and TME remodeling. The study emphasizes their potential to improve antitumor immunity and synergize with existing immunotherapies in preclinical models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Co-expression of multiple immunomodulatory transgenes enhances dendritic cell maturation and CD8+ T cell infiltration in tumors",
    "Multi-transgene OVs remodel immunosuppressive tumor microenvironments and improve effector-to-regulatory T cell ratios",
    "These Ousing OVs synergize with immune checkpoint inhibitors and adoptive cell therapies in preclinical settings"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes multi-transgene-armed oncolytic viruses as a promising strategy to overcome tumor immunosuppression through coordinated immune activation, advancing the design of next-generation cancer immunotherapies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the intrinsic inefficiency of Fe single-atom catalysts (Fe-N4) by engineering carbon defects adjacent to Fe sites using bismuth-mediated zinc extraction from ZIF-8. The Fe-N-pCd catalyst achieved a high half-wave potential of 0.918 V vs. RHE in alkaline electrolytes and demonstrated stable Zn-air battery operation beyond 3000 hours at -40°C. Defects redistributed electron density, favoring an axial *OH-bound Fe state and accelerating oxygen reduction kinetics by altering the rate-limiting step.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Bismuth-mediated zinc extraction creates carbon defects adjacent to Fe-N4 sites on ZIF-8-derived carbon",
    "Fe-N-pCd catalyst achieved 0.918 V half-wave potential vs. RHE in alkaline electrolytes",
    "Quasi-solid-state Zn-air battery with Fe-N-pCd cathode operated stably for over 3000 hours at -40°C"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a defect engineering strategy to optimize single-atom catalyst microenvironments, enhancing oxygen reduction kinetics by modifying electronic structure and reaction pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated transcriptomic differences between pseudoexfoliation syndrome (PEX), pseudoex. glaucoma (PXG), and control blood samples to identify potential biomarkers. Using RNA-seq and validation via RT-qPCR, three candidate biomarkers (ACTA2, IL1RN, MMP9) were identified. These genes were associated with actin cytoskeleton regulation and leukocyte transendothelial migration pathways. The biomarkers showed differential expression across PEX and PXG groups, suggesting molecular alterations in pseudoexfoliation pathology.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Three candidate biomarkers (ACTA2, IL1RN, MMP9) were identified through transcriptome sequencing of blood samples from PEX, PXG, and control groups.",
    "Gene set enrichment analysis linked the biomarkers to actin cytoskeleton regulation and leukocyte transendothelial migration pathways.",
    "RT-qPCR validation confirmed significant upregulation of ACTA2 and MMP9 in PXG patients versus controls, with elevated levels in PEX patients compared to both controls and PXG."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The identification of these biomarkers provides potential molecular targets for understanding pseudoexfoliation glaucoma pathophysiology and may inform future therapeutic strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses cryoprotectant selection challenges by leveraging pretrained language models to encode small-molecule structures as SMILES sequences. The approach prioritized candidates through hierarchical representations, descriptor reconstruction, and prediction of ice recrystallization metrics. Experimental validation in red blood cells, stem cells, and tissues showed improved cryopreservation outcomes with selected additives, demonstrating a computational screening method linking molecular properties to functional cryobiological endpoints.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Pretrained language models encoded small-molecule structures to prioritize cryoprotectant candidates",
    "Predicted ice recrystusing normalized mean grain size and thresholded labels",
    "Selected additives enhanced cryopreservation recovery in red blood cells, stem cells, and tissues"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a computational framework for predicting cryoprotectant efficacy across multiple biological scales, bridging molecular property prediction with experimental cryobiology outcomes."
}

{
  "summary": "This review investigates the mechanisms driving renal allograft fibrosis post-transplantation, focusing on immune cell contributions. It analyzes how innate and adaptive immune responses transition injury to chronic remodeling, emphasizing cellular plasticity and communication. Human studies reveal dynamic networks of immune and stromal cells rather than static pathogenic populations. Current immunosuppression prevents injury, but emerging therapies like regulatory T cell modulation and cytokine blockade remain investigational without proven efficacy against established fibrosis.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Renal allograft fibrosis results from multiple injury pathways converging on interstitial fibrosis and tubular atusing",
    "Human single-cell and spatial analyses indicate heterogeneous, stage-dependent immune-stromal networks rather than fixed pathogenic cell populations",
    "Emerging immunomodulatory therapies lack proven efficacy in reversing established allograft fibrosis"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work clarifies the dynamic immune-stromal interactions in renal allograft fibrosis, providing a foundation for targeted interventions to prevent progression while highlighting the need for integrated diagnostic and therapeutic strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing terahertz hyperspectral imaging using high-density pixelated metasurfaces. The approach leverages photonic crystal heterojunctions to create pixelated metasurfaces that encode spatial information into spectrally resolved resonances. Key results include suppressing lateral leakage, enabling three-dimensional photon confinement, and achieving nine independently addressable resonances in a single 3×3 pixel array. The system operates with a single-pixel detector and THz pulse, eliminating raster scanning and computational reconstruction.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Pixelated metasurfaces with ∼2λ lateral dimensions retain high spectral fidelity and signal-to-noise ratio",
    "Three-dimensional photon confinement enables enhanced quality factors without increasing device footprint",
    "Single-shot broadband terahertz measurement retrieves nine independently addressable resonances"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a direct spectral-spatial encoding mechanism for terahertz hyperspectral imaging, overcoming traditional limitations in spatial resolution, spectral sampling, and computational requirements."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how SARS-CoV-2 infection disrupts hematopoiesis, focusing on hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells (HSPCs) and mature blood cells. It identifies ACE2 and TMPRSS2 expression in rare HSPC precursors, suggesting injury may stem from spike protein and inflammatory mediators rather than direct viral infection. Key mechanisms include NLRP3 inflammasome activation, pyroptosis, senescence, epigenetic changes, and niche remodeling. These lead to lymphopenia, thrombocytopenia, coagulopathy, and anemia, which can persist post-viral clearance. The findings inform clinical management strategies and vaccination benefits.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SARS-CoV-2 infection causes hematopoietic injury via non-infectious mechanisms involving spike protein and inflammatory mediators rather than direct viral infection in HSPCs",
    "Mechanisms include NLRP3 inflammasome activation, pyroptosis, senescence, epigenetic reprogramming, and bone marrow niche remodeling",
    "Hematological abnormalities such as lymphopenia, thrombocytopenia, coagulopathy, and anemia persist post-viral clearance in some patients"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work elucidates the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying SARS-CoV-2-induced hematopoietic dysfunction, providing critical insights for understanding long-term hematological complications and guiding targeted therapeutic interventions."
}

{
  "summary": "Articular cartilage defects pose significant repair challenges due to limited self-repair capacity. This study developed a dynamically adaptive wet-adhesive hydrogel (OHA/QCS/SF) to enhance interface healing. The hydrogel demonstrated rapid underwater spreading, fluid displacement, and infiltration into cartilage interfaces. It promoted wet adhesion via dynamic Schiff-base bonding and self-healing under mechanical stress. In rabbit models, it improved defect filling, host-graft integration, and cartilage regeneration when loaded with synovial membrane-derived mesenchymal stem cells.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The hydrogel exhibited rapid underwater spreading and fluid displacement at cartilage interfaces",
    "Dynamic Schiff-base bonding enabled wet adhesion and self-healing under mechanical stress",
    "In rabbit cartilage defects, the hydrogel with SMSCs enhanced defect filling and host-graft integration"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a dynamic wet-adhesive hydrogel strategy for improving biomaterial-cartilage interface healing in fluid-rich joint environments, addressing a critical barrier to effective cartilage repair."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated Treg heterogeneity in colorectal cancer liver metastases (CRLM) using single-cell transcriptomics and experimental validation. It identified a shift toward CCR8+ effector Tregs with immunosuppressive traits, linked to CXCL16-CXCR6 signaling. In vitro assays showed CCR8+ Tregs migrate toward CXCL16, and CXCR6 blockade reduced this response. Human CRLM samples correlated CCR8+ Treg enrichment with reduced effector T cells and increased inhibitory checkpoints, suggesting CXCL16-CXCR6 drives immunosuppressive microenvironment formation in CRLM.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CXCL16-CXCR6 signaling promotes CCR8+ effector Treg accumulation in colorectal cancer liver metastases",
    "CCR8+ effector Tregs in CRLM show reduced effector T-cell abundance and elevated inhibitory checkpoint expression",
    "CXCR6 blockade attenuates CXCL16-mediated chemotaxis of CCR8+ Tregs in vitro"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes CXCL16-CXCR6 as a key axis driving immunosuppressive Treg enrichment in colorectal cancer liver metastases, revealing a mechanism for metastatic niche immunosuppression."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the need for adaptive luminescent materials in extreme environments by developing solvent-free ionic liquids with enhanced photoluminescence quantum yield (PLQY). Using supramolecular locking via anion-π+ interactions, researchers achieved 80% PLQ. The materials retained high emission under thermal stress (up to 400°C), vacuum (250°C), and acidic/basic conditions, demonstrating exceptional robustness while maintaining fluidity. This approach enables durable photonic applications in harsh conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "80% photoluminescence quantum yield in liquid state",
    "Thermal stability up to 400°C",
    "Resistance to acidic and basic environments without degradation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a molecular design strategy for highly robust, emissive liquid fluorophores that overcome aggregation-caused quenching and nonradiative decay, enabling photonic technologies in extreme environments."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether neonatal mesenchymal stem cells and their secretome could improve diastolic function in heart failure with preserved ejection fraction (HFpEF) mice. Using a causal machine learning framework, the researchers identified regulatory T cells as key mediators of cardiac remodeling. The treatment reduced inflammation and fibrosis while expanding regulatory T cells, leading to improved diastolic function in HFp. The findings suggest a potential therapeutic target for HFpEF.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Neonatal mesenchymal stem cells and their secretome improved diastolic function in HFpEF mice",
    "Regulatory T cells were expanded and mediated cardiac remodeling improvements",
    "The treatment reduced inflammation and fibrosis in the heart"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies regulatory T cells as a causal mechanism for diastolic function improvement in HFpEF, providing a novel therapeutic target for heart failure with preserved ejection fraction."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the limitation of single-channel signal transduction in artificial vision systems by developing a retinomorphic device using carbon nanotube/zinc oxide heterostructured nanotubes. The device generates dual ionic and electronic signals upon optical stimulation, mimicking biological reticulate phototransduction. It achieves 96.5% luminance adaptation and 98.2% color discrimination accuracy, demonstrating potential for embodied intelligence applications through real-world navigation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The device produces distinct ionic and electronic current signals upon light exposure",
    "It achieves 96.5% luminance adaptation and 98.2% color discrimination accuracy",
    "Real-world traffic-light guided navigation validates its application in embodied intelligence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a dual-channel signal transduction mechanism in a single device that mimics biological retinal parallel processing, advancing artificial vision systems beyond conventional single-channel approaches."
}
